      "dom_id": "question-182495",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Simplify the statement $¬(¬R⇒S).$",
      "worked_solution": "The conditional statement $P⇒Q$ is logically equivalent to the disjunction $¬P∨Q:$\n\nSo, in this case, we have the following equivalence:\n\n$$\n¬(¬R⇒S)≡¬(¬(¬R)∨S)\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negation, we have\n\n$$\n¬(¬(¬R)∨S)≡¬(R∨S).\n$$\n\nDistributing the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(R∨S)≡¬R∧¬S.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $¬R∧¬S.$",
